## 6. Writing requirements (academic voice, measured)
README.md (≈1,200–1,800 words):
1. Title + one-line takeaway.
2. Abstract (≤150 words): question, data, method, result with magnitudes, caveat.
3. Why this matters: link to the BIS Annual Economic Report 2025 discussion of stablecoins and the Act's reserve rule — two paragraphs, no hype.
4. Data: sources, universe, timing convention, sample dates, N.
5. Method: equation, controls, inference, link to PAP.md.
6. Results: primary (fig1, table1); term structure (fig2); asymmetry (fig4). Always give economic magnitudes, e.g. "a USD 10 bn 5-day inflow is associated with X bp (90% CI a to b) lower 3-month yields after 10 days pre-enactment versus Y bp post-enactment; the difference is / is not statistically distinguishable from zero."
7. Robustness: table2, one paragraph.
8. What this does NOT show: endogeneity of flows (rates → stablecoin demand; risk-on/off), short post sample and low power, Act not yet binding, DefiLlama measurement, overlapping-horizon inference. We list our weaknesses before anyone else does.
9. Relation to Ahmed & Aldasoro (2025): what we replicate, what differs, what we add.
10. Reproduce: `make all`; data vintage date.
11. References: Ahmed & Aldasoro (2025) BIS WP [VERIFY no.]; BIS Annual Economic Report 2025, stablecoin chapter [VERIFY chapter]; Jordà (2005); Newey & West (1987); GENIUS Act, Public Law 119-27 [VERIFY].

docs/LINKEDIN.md (≤1,500 characters, English): line 1 is a hook containing the key number; one sentence on what the GENIUS Act requires; three short findings with magnitudes; one sentence of limitations; "Code + data: https://github.com/<my-handle>/stablecoin-tbills-genius-act"; credit the anchor paper and name its authors (I will tag them); at most one emoji; hashtags #stablecoins #Treasuries #BIS #monetarypolicy. Add two lines of alt-text for the chart.

docs/SUMMARY_TH.md: a 10-line Thai summary of findings and caveats for me.

Language rules: never write "stablecoins cause…"; use "is associated with", "consistent with", "we cannot rule out". Quantify every claim. No words like "massive" or "game-changing".

## 7. Default decisions (assume these; do not ask)
- If DefiLlama history starts after 2021-01-01, use what exists and say so.
- Gaps in a coin's history: forward-fill ≤3 days and log; longer gaps → NaN, excluded from the aggregate on those dates, logged.
- If the post sample has <200 business days, still run everything and add a power warning to the note.
- If results are null or opposite-signed, that is the headline; write it as such.
- If web access is unavailable, keep every [VERIFY] item listed in README under "To verify before publication" and tell me at the end.

## 8. First action
Echo back a plan of ≤15 lines (data sources, universe, primary spec, checkpoints), then start Phase 0 immediately. No clarifying questions unless something is truly blocking.
